Wearing a mask can be used as the first stage of defense to reduce the risk of infection; the use of Surgical masks and N95 respiratory masks (Series #1860s) helps control the spread of viruses.
Surgical face mask prevents small droplets of fluid from a potentially infected person through the air or getting stuck on the surface of the object, from which they could spread to others.
However, only N95 (seriges #1860s) masks can be protected from intructing small virons such as 10 to 80 nm, only 5% virons are able to fully enter; SARS-CoV-2 size is equal to SARS-COVCoV and both are about £85 nm.
Since particles can even enter through a surgical mask, health care providers who come in direct contact with patients must not wear a surgical mask (Series #1860s).
In addition to masks for health care providers to further reduce contact with the virus, fit isolation gowns should be worn.
The virus can also inflict people through the eyes.
On January 22, 2020, a doctor was infected with SARS-CoV-2 even though he was wearing an N95 mask; the virus probably entered his body through his inflammatory eyes.
Thus, healthcare providers should also wear transparent face coverings or goggles when patients are working.
In people's cases in affected or potentially affected areas, everyone is advised to wash their hands with more frequent disinfectant soaps more frequently than usual, trying to stay indoors to quarantine themselves, and to limit exposure to potentially infected people.
A three-feeth distance is considered suitable for people to stay away from a patient.
These measures are effective methods to reduce the risk of infection as well as to prevent the spread of the virus.
Although the SARS-CoV-2 came as a new virus in the human class world, due to its high resemblance with SARS-COV on January 7th, according to a report on January 7, 2020, China's high precautions should have been taken based on deep memories of the SARS outpre occasion.
