This message significantly eased public fears, especially when the whole country was preparing for the Spring Festivities and was a waste of crucial time to suppress the disease at a minimal level in Wuhan.
China's diagnosid agencies can receive this stricken education and lead to essential improvements in the future.
For example, these organizations will need to be more careful when declaring (1) publicly because every word citizens will consider and it can change their attitudes and decisions; ((2) to be more sensitive and responsive to undesirable information received from clinics without waiting for formal reports of physicians or officials; (3) instead of trying to comfort the public; and (4) to raise public awareness about epidemic diseases and periodically to test and improve society's response procedures.
The COVID-19 outbreak caused by SARS-CoV-2 began at the end of December 2019.
