Ten years later, an outcruption of Middle Eastern Respiratory Syndrome (MERS) epidemics continued in the Arabian peninsuls and sporadically spread to the rest of the world.
2019 Novel HCoV (2019-nCoV), which was subsequently renamed SARS-CoV-2, an effective agent for the current pandemic 2019 (COVID-19), resulted in the death of more than 3,120 people as of March 3, 2020 and infected more than 91,000 people.
