On 6 February 2020, our team published a quick consultation guide for the detection and treatment of Novel Coronavirus 2019 (2019-nCOVOV) infection, and this guidance gave us experience and made good references for the fight against this pandemic worldwide.
However, Corona Virus Disease 2019 (COVIID-19) is also gradually increasing our awareness and knowledge based based on a new disease, ongoing research findings and clinical practice experiences; therefore, diagnosis and medical techniques are also constantly being updated.
In this letter, we responded to a comment on our directives and, according to the latest COVID-in-religation and treatment guidelines issued by the National Health Committee of the People’s Republic of China, “Suspiced Cases” and “Confirmed Cases”.”
In December 2019, the Novel Coronavirus (2019-nCoV) was officially named Coronavirus Disease 2019 (COVID-19) and the virus was renamed Civier Acute Respiratory Syndrome (SARS-CoV-2).
On March 11, 2020, WHO identified COVID-19 as a pandemic.
In order to combat SARS-CoV-2 infection, our team has developed a quick consultation guideline and it has been published on 06 February 2020 at Military Medical Research Online.
Since it was published, there has been a huge response.
Keep in mind, COVID-19 is also gradually increasing our awareness and knowledge based on a new disease, ongoing research findings, and clinical practice experience; therefore, diagnosis and medical techniques are also constantly being updated.
For example, COVID-related diagnosis and medical instructions (http://www.nhc.gov.cn/) issued by the National Health Committee of the People's People's People's People's Republic of Chineg (http://www.nhc.gov.cn/), between 16 January 2020 and 3 March 2020, a total of seven editions have been released, each of which has made significant changes to some content.
Now Zhou and his associates have made a comment about our guidance, they have offered to set a simple score based on their clinical experience.
Their work has added new evidence to our guidance and has also made valuable references for this global pandemic.
We will continue to provide significant work and thank you.
However, according to the most recent diagnosis and medical guidelines of COVID-19 (Trial Seventh Edition) and recent research, their work will also need to be updated.
According to the 7th edition (March 2020), to confirm the suspected case, one of the epidemiological historical traities for a detailed analysation must have two clinical prefixes, or if there is no clear epidemiological history, it is necessary to meet three clinical symptoms.
Epidemiological history: ((1) the history of those residents of Wuhan city and its vicinal areas, or other communities where COVID-19 cases have been reported in the last 14 daies before the symptoms manifest; (2) a history of exposure to SARS-VCoV-2 infectious cases (positive access to nucleic acid test); (3) a history of exposure to patients with fever or respiratory symptoms in Wuhan city or surrounding areas, or other communities have been reported of COVID-19 cases in the last 14 days before the symptoms appear.
Clinical releases: (1) fever and/or respiratory symptoms; (2) with imaging characteristics of COVID-19 infections; (3) Total white blood cell counts at an early stating stage demonstrate normal, reduced or reduced lymphocycyte count.
To diagnose confirmed cases based on suspected cases, there should be pathogenic or serological evidence below: (1) SARS-VCoV-reculative real-tem-te-perminatory PCR tested positive; (2) obtained high homogenity or mill with the known novel corona virus in full gene sequencing of the virus; (3) Serum test results from certain IgM antibodies of SARS-CoV-2 and IgG antibodies.
We have found that nucleic acid cereal time PCR tests and blood samples have been included in the second (18 January 2020) edition (22 January 2020).
The pathological detection of blood samples was added to the fourth (27 January 2020) and the fifth (February 2020); and the cereological evidence was added to the 7th edition.
Depending on the continued work of the researchers, these changes to quickly diagnosize a favorable nucleic acid detection kit with respiratory duct samples, which increase the invalence of different samples and which helps to come up with certain antibody positive results.
Moreover, there has been more evidence, which reminds us to be cautious about patients with irregular symptoms and asymptomatic.
Therefore, the flow list of Zhou and his companions should be updated, as they have classified individuals who do not have clinical symptoms “low-prived”.”
It is also necessary to verify in subsequent clinical practices and studies.
As a conclusion, we hope that there will come more direct evidence and readers will call for their comments.
To dedicate “impossible” and “confirmed cases”, we recommend identifying them and following our country’s “reconcissible”.”
Our team will continue to update on time to help.
Five new deaths have been reported due to COVID-19.
Yesterday, Bangladesh confirmed five new deaths due to COVID-19.
This is the highest death toll due to the virus.
The Institute of Epidemiology, Disease Control and Research (IEDCR) in Bangladesh yesterday said that the number of infected cases recorded included 114 active cases and 33 of those recovering.
A total of 17 deaths have been recorded.
IEDCR Director Dr Meerjady Sabrina Flora said the deaths included four men and a woman.
According to Dr. Mirzadi, two cases are over the age of 60, between the ages of 51 and 60, and one is 41-50.
He added that two of the victims were from Dhaka.
The World Health Organization (WHO) declared COVID-19 a pandemic on March 11.
Jalal Saifur Rahman, one of the victims of the deceased was Jalal Saifur Rahman, a director of the Bangla Anti-Corruption Commission, who was served at Kuwait Friendship Hospital.
On Saturday, Bangladesh Road Transport and Bridges Minister Obaidul Quader said that public transport will remain closed for longer than planned until next Saturday.
